# =============================================================================
# .trivyignore - Trivy vulnerability exceptions
# =============================================================================
# Format: CVE-ID [expiry-date] # reason
# Expiry dates enforce periodic re-review.
# All entries must document: affected package, why it cannot be fixed,
# and the actual risk in this deployment context.
# =============================================================================

# CVE-2026-0994 | protobuf | CVSS 8.2 HIGH
# Affected:  google.protobuf.json_format.ParseDict() - uncontrolled recursion
#            via deeply nested google.protobuf.Any messages -> DoS
# Why not fixed: opentelemetry-proto==1.27.0 (transitive via
#   opentelemetry-exporter-otlp-proto-grpc==1.27.0) caps protobuf at <5.0.
#   Pinning protobuf>=5.29.6 causes ResolutionImpossible breaking all installs.
# Actual risk: LOW in this context.
#   - ParseDict() is not called anywhere in application code
#   - protobuf used exclusively for gRPC OTLP telemetry transport
#   - No attacker-controlled input reaches protobuf deserialization
# Remediation path: upgrade otel SDK to protobuf-5.x-compatible release
# Review by: 2026-08-24
CVE-2026-0994
